  "description": "<div>\n<p>Return the entries of a rectangular matrix in clockwise spiral order, beginning at the upper-left corner and peeling one perimeter at a time. Stop once each cell has been visited exactly once; thin inner layers need special care.</p>\n<p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> matrix = [[1,2,3],[4,5,6],[7,8,9]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [1,2,3,6,9,8,7,4,5]\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> Read the outer ring clockwise, then the center.</pre>\n<p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> matrix = [[1,2,3,4]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [1,2,3,4]\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> A single row is already in spiral order.</pre>\n<p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> matrix = []\n<strong>Output:</strong> []\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> There are no cells to visit.</pre>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>0 &lt;= matrix.length &lt;= 10</code>.</li>\n<li>If the matrix is nonempty, <code>1 &lt;= matrix[0].length &lt;= 10</code> and all rows have that length.</li>\n<li>Each entry is an integer in <code>[-1000, 1000]</code>.</li>\n<li>An empty matrix produces an empty array.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>",
